# The feature flags of the STAGING web service (sme-web), one KEY=VALUE per line (owner, 9 Nov 2026).
# `make deploy-staging WHAT=web` applies them with --update-env-vars on every deploy, so a redeploy or a recreated service can never lose them.
#   SPEAKS_PANEL_SCREENS=1 (11 Nov 2026): "How your assistant speaks" reads and saves through C1's endpoint (on staging since #463), no longer the browser mock.
#   REQUEST_MEMO=1 (12 Nov 2026): an identical read of the API inside one page render is asked once (lib/api/request-memo.ts); off = every read is asked.
#   TEST_CALL_TONE=1 (12 Nov 2026, owner's A3): the Tone choice (Respectful, Friendly, Casual) on "Place a test call"; the API takes `tone` on POST /calls/place since e0c137ab (docs/contracts/calls.md). Staging only; production never reads this file.
#   TODAY_SUMMARY_SCREENS=1 (12 Nov 2026): the Today page asks C1's one GET /today/summary instead of about 25 reads (lib/api/today-summary.ts); off = Today asks its own routes.
#   OUTBOX_WHATSAPP=1 (13 Nov 2026, owner's C10; was mock until C1's #538 mark-sent route was live on staging as sme-api-00165-hw9): "Open in WhatsApp" and "I sent it" on an approved Outbox message (Owner and Admin). The button opens the owner's own WhatsApp (this system sends nothing); "I sent it" calls C1's POST /outbox/messages/{id}/mark-sent (`mock` would record nothing). Production never sets it.
#   LEGAL_DRAFT_PAGES=1 (13 Nov 2026, owner's D13): the DRAFT legal pages (today /refund-policy) exist for the owner to read; a plain 404 everywhere else. Never indexed.
#   TODAY_V5=1 (13 Nov 2026, decided by C2): "quiet Today": the team strip and the totals after calls are folded under one line, "More on Today" (needs APP_V4). Off = Today as before.
#   DESIGN_V6=1 (13 Nov 2026, owner's DESIGN SYSTEM + ALL PAGES): the new look (cream + dots + orange glow in light, brown-black + grid in dark), the new short side menu and the new pages; BALANCE_SCREENS=mock = a made-up ₹1,550 on the business card until C1's billing v2; ASSISTANT_STATUS=mock = the assistant's state kept in a cookie until C1's route. Needs APP_V4.
#   OWNER_TALK_PREFS=mock (14 Nov 2026, owner item G): "How it talks to you" in My assistant > Voice & tone (voice, style, what it calls you, words, speed; per person): the choices sit in a cookie of the browser and no sound is made until C1's /v1/me/talk-prefs is on staging, then `1`. Needs DESIGN_V6.
#   CALL_LIMIT_SCREENS=1 (was mock until C1's API 00178 was on staging; 14 Nov 2026, owner decision): "Calls per day" in My assistant > Rules (the business's own limit on the calls its assistant makes in a day, default 100, 1 to 5000; the Owner changes it after one question); `mock` = a test version that keeps the number in this browser until C1's `/tasks/call-limit` is on staging, then `1`. Production: unset (the card is not there).
#   TEACH_SCREENS=mock (13 Nov 2026): "Teach this" on assistant lines (calls, chats, practice): the corrected answer is kept in a cookie of the browser until C1's POST /knowledge/corrections exists. Needs DESIGN_V6.
#   CHAT_ASSISTANT_SWITCH=mock (13 Nov 2026): the per-chat "Assistant: on/off" switch on the Chats page; the owner's choice is kept in a cookie of the browser until C1 can save it. Needs DESIGN_V6.
#   RAZORPAY_CHECKOUT=1 (13 Nov 2026, owner's C9): before a plan starts the web asks the API for a checkout session (C1's POST /billing/checkout); with the fake provider (staging today) or an API without the route it falls back to the three test payment choices; the Razorpay addresses are in the page rules only while this is 1. Real Razorpay needs the owner's TEST keys on the API.
#   PHONE_NUMBER_SCREENS=mock (13 Nov 2026, owner's B6): Settings > Phone number: pick a city, a made-up number is reserved, the approval steps, a test ring; kept in a cookie of the browser, nothing bought, rented or rung (C1's API does not exist yet).
#   13 Nov 2026 (C1's routes are on staging, sme-api-00166-b4h): ASSISTANT_STATUS, BALANCE_SCREENS and TEACH_SCREENS are 1 (the real routes: assistant status and go-live/pause, balance v2, knowledge corrections with undo). PLAN_SCREENS and TOPUP_SCREENS stay 0: the old v1 trial routes answer 404 while PRICING_V2 is on.
#   STAFF_CONSOLE=mock (13 Nov 2026, decided by C2): the staff console at /staff (Overview, support view of a business) shows a fixed realistic sample (a saree-shop set; ?role=owner, support or finance switches the role) until a staff account exists; `1` = C1's /v1/admin API. Production never sets it (the area is then a plain 404).
#   BOOTSTRAP=1 (12 Nov 2026, owner approved Phase 1): the workspace layout reads through C1's one GET /bootstrap (lib/api/bootstrap.ts); off = every read asks its own route.
#   PLAN_SCREENS=0 and TOPUP_SCREENS=0 (13 Nov 2026, owner's check before the staging deploy; decided by C1): the v1 plan screens (30-day trial, Starter/Growth/Business, minute packs) say things the final pricing replaced (a trial, "100 minutes"). While PRICING_V2 is on the API (it closes the v1 trial, resume, checkout, upgrade and pack top-up routes with a 404), these two stay off here; C2's billing screens (balance in rupees, free start, orders) replace them.
#   DEVELOPER_KEYS_SCREENS=1 (13 Nov 2026, owner's Settings page; C1's /developer/keys and /developer/usage routes, docs/contracts/developer-api.md): Settings > Developer API keys makes, rotates and revokes TEST keys (a secret is shown once, never stored) and shows the test usage. Needs DESIGN_V6; Owner and Admin. Live keys do not exist.
#   BILLING_V2 (19 Nov 2026, OWNER TO DECIDE, not set here): the Billing page as one rupee wallet with usage per feature, limits, warnings and the upgrade hint. `BILLING_V2=mock` shows it with made-up numbers marked "Preview" (?demo=low80|full100|over|upgrade|numbers); `1` reads C1 where the routes exist. Paid plans start in Feb 2027, so leave it unset until the owner wants to see it.
# STAGING ONLY: production (sme-site) is deployed separately and never reads this file. Not a secret: flags and workspace ids only. Change a value here, then deploy.
#   AI_TEAM_SCREENS=1 and ABOUT_BUSINESS_SCREENS=1 (owner, 9 Nov 2026): the AI team page (day, panel, text stand-up) and About my business read the real API. AUTO_REPLY_SCREENS stays mock: the staging worker has no auto-reply switch or model key.
#   CALL_SCREENS / OUTCOME_SCREENS / PLAN_SCREENS = 1 (owner, 9 Nov 2026): the live-call screen, call outcomes and plan & usage read the real API. MARKS_SCREENS and OWN_VOICE_SCREENS stay OFF (they send real messages / clone a voice).
ABOUT_BUSINESS_SCREENS=1
ACTIVITY_SCREENS=1
ASSISTANT_STATUS=1
BALANCE_SCREENS=1
CHAT_ASSISTANT_SWITCH=1
DESIGN_V6=1
AI_TEAM_SCREENS=1
APP_V4=1
ASSISTANT_SCREENS=1
ASSISTANT_WORK_SCREENS=1
ASSISTANT_WORK_TENANTS=c029cba3-d2f8-4923-8c5a-630852797fd3;7013c5ff-7f60-4b9e-ba9b-ac7bbc32651e;5717d629-9289-4480-b895-59abb65ce2ce;63e9ce7f-1343-45c3-b3d4-2c1f59253aae;e00d4db1-2c99-46a9-a273-07b9b9ff764c;b3de0526-239c-4104-a4b8-e82d7bac41d2;a207d1ff-0380-41bd-8ea3-36ec5250de05;6cad34c2-6d54-407c-85cc-e3c959e0b45b;d9dbd3d5-0d9d-4f78-854e-29d9bdaada35;da772041-0726-49ae-9885-28e4c534f775
AUTO_REPLY_SCREENS=mock
BOOTSTRAP=1
BROWSER_VOICE=1
CALL_SCREENS=1
CALL_SETTINGS_SCREENS=1
DEVELOPER_KEYS_SCREENS=1
DPDP_SCREENS=1
GUIDED_DEMO=1
DEMO_CALL=1
LEADS_SCREENS=1
LEGAL_DRAFT_PAGES=1
OPENING_LINE_SCREENS=1
OUTBOX_WHATSAPP=1
OUTCOME_SCREENS=1
OUTREACH_SCREENS=1
OWNER_TALK_PREFS=mock
CALL_LIMIT_SCREENS=1
PHONE_NUMBER_SCREENS=mock
PLAN_SCREENS=0
PRONUNCIATION_SCREENS=1
RAZORPAY_CHECKOUT=1
REQUEST_MEMO=1
SOURCE_CARDS_SCREENS=1
SPEAKS_PANEL_SCREENS=1
STAFF_CONSOLE=1
SWEEP_SCREENS=mock
TALK_TRAINING_SCREENS=1
TASK_SCREENS=1
TEACH_SCREENS=1
TEST_CALL_SCREENS=1
TEST_CALL_TONE=1
TODAY_SUMMARY_SCREENS=1
TODAY_V5=1
TOPUP_SCREENS=0
VOICE_PICKER_SCREENS=1
VOICE_SAMPLE_SCREENS=1
WAITLIST=mock
OFFER_SCREENS=1
# PREVIEW_JOBS=1 (19 Nov 2026, C2): staging only: /app/preview turns the JOBS and BILLING_V2 screens on with sample data for ONE browser (a cookie); nobody else sees a change. Never set in production (the production build ignores the cookie).
PREVIEW_JOBS=1
# 25 Nov 2026 (C2): two flags the live staging service already had but this file did not name (a deploy added JOBS by hand each time): JOBS = the Jobs screens (owner decision 19 Nov), CHAT_QUEUE_SCREENS = the Chats composer queue (19 Nov). The file now says what the service runs.
JOBS=1
CHAT_QUEUE_SCREENS=1
# 25 Nov 2026 (C2): first run by business type: a workspace made without a type is asked once on Get started (PUT /pack, C1's first-run contract; the API route lands with C1's #1066). Staging only until the owner has seen it.
FIRST_RUN_TYPE=1
# 25 Nov 2026 (C2): My assistant in the open layout (two tabs, hairline sections, extras under More choices): staging first, the owner chose the layout on 24 Nov. NOT in production until he has seen it.
MY_ASSISTANT_OPEN=1
# 25 Nov 2026 (C2): Phone numbers as three plain steps.
# 25 Nov 2026 (C2): Settings (Business) and Team (people, invite) as plain labelled fields, one Save.
SETTINGS_OPEN=1
# 25 Nov 2026 (C2): Today in the open look (category-coloured bare icons, one orange action per row, no boxes for empty notes).
TODAY_OPEN=1
# 25 Nov 2026 (C2): the First day page in the open layout (no ring, no cards, one Start button). Staging first; production after the owner has seen it.
FIRST_DAY_OPEN=1
# 25 Nov 2026 (C2): Chats > Messages we send as plain rows, ONE Send all for approval.
TEMPLATES_PLAIN=1
# 25 Nov 2026 (C2): filters without sentences (Calls, Leads, Reports period, Catalogue).
FILTERS_OPEN=1
# 25 Nov 2026 (C2): Calls as a list (who, one sentence, when).
CALLS_OPEN=1
# 25 Nov 2026 (C2): Leads as an open list.
LEADS_OPEN=1
# 25 Nov 2026 (C2): Reports as one calm page (3 numbers, a sentence, one chart, More reports).
REPORTS_OPEN=1
# 25 Nov 2026 (C2): the industry pages /for/<industry> (English only).
INDUSTRY_PAGES=1
# 28 Nov 2026 (C2): the number picker (pick your own business number). `mock` = made-up numbers, nothing is bought. Not in production until C1's routes are live.
PHONE_PICKER=mock
# 29 Nov 2026 (C2): "Tell your assistant what to do" on Jobs (describe the job in your own words, see a draft, turn it on). `mock` = a made-up reading; nothing is sent to the model.
TELL_SCREENS=mock
# 29 Nov 2026 (C2): Get a phone number in four steps and Verify your business (the business's own account; needs PHONE_PICKER too). `mock` = made-up status in a cookie, nothing is sent.
KYC_PER_CLIENT=mock
